1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,600
[Episode 24]

3
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:24,310
Over there!

4
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:25,230
Go!

5
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:40,150
Where are the others?
Hurry!

6
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:41,920
Head upstream along the river.
They...

7
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,710
They're going to kill everyone.

8
00:01:43,710 --> 00:01:44,280
Go now!

9
00:01:44,710 --> 00:01:45,560
Get her into the ambulance.

10
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:46,640
Go!

11
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:52,640
Hurry!

12
00:01:57,870 --> 00:01:59,640
Hurry if you want to live.

13
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,470
How much longer
until Old He's team arrives?

14
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,030
They're on the way.
A few more minutes.

15
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:23,520
There's no time.

16
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:24,960
Police!
Freeze!

17
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:34,870
You two, go around that side.

18
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:35,710
Flank them.

19
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:41,680
Captain Ren.

20
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:45,960
Chen Wenji is inside.

21
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:46,560
Go!

22
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:43,590
Uncle He.
How is it?

23
00:03:45,470 --> 00:03:46,310
Chen Wenji!

24
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:54,520
Get down now!

25
00:03:58,710 --> 00:03:59,280
Chen Wenji!

26
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,520
Listen to me.

27
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:03,520
This place is surrounded by police.

28
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:05,910
You can't escape again.

29
00:04:06,310 --> 00:04:07,560
You're about to tell me

30
00:04:07,590 --> 00:04:09,590
to drop my weapon
and seek lenient treatment?

31
00:04:09,910 --> 00:04:11,520
Save it.

32
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,470
I'm dead either way today.

33
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,360
I lived seven extra years.

34
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,720
I came out ahead.

35
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:23,070
You know exactly
how you lived those seven years.

36
00:04:23,070 --> 00:04:25,720
You were worse off than a sewer rat.

37
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:31,070
Your life wasn't much better.

38
00:04:31,510 --> 00:04:33,430
You couldn't sleep at night, could you?

39
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:34,510
Feeling guilty?

40
00:05:18,830 --> 00:05:19,870
Go on.
Shoot.

41
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:22,950
Isn't this the day you longed for?

42
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:48,830
You are

43
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:50,160
Han Shuang.

44
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:56,160
Welcome back.

45
00:06:20,950 --> 00:06:23,160
You will face justice under the law.

46
00:06:33,870 --> 00:06:34,680
Fan Zhichang.

47
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:38,360
You stood by and watched
your own mother die.

48
00:06:39,830 --> 00:06:41,430
You also betrayed your own brother

49
00:06:42,480 --> 00:06:44,560
and even killed your only nephew.

50
00:06:45,950 --> 00:06:47,310
But none of that matters to you.

51
00:06:47,870 --> 00:06:48,390
None of it.

52
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,600
What matters is

53
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,430
you lost

54
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,160
the ability to have children.

55
00:06:59,510 --> 00:07:01,510
By the time you realized how badly
childhood bullying had harmed you,

56
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:04,750
it was already too late.

57
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,560
Even after you became a doctor,

58
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:10,950
your pride and sensitivity
kept you from accepting it.

59
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:13,560
Nonsense.

60
00:07:14,070 --> 00:07:15,390
You didn't dare tell anyone.

61
00:07:16,510 --> 00:07:18,040
You didn't dare see a doctor either.

62
00:07:19,510 --> 00:07:21,630
So you chose to deceive yourself.

63
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:24,800
Even your own wife
didn't dare express concern.

64
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,560
You feared that if others knew,

65
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,000
they would mock you,

66
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:31,950
a high-and-mighty expert and professor.

67
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,270
Shut up!

68
00:07:33,270 --> 00:07:34,000
Sit down.

69
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,830
After you met Xiao Ting,

70
00:07:54,430 --> 00:07:56,040
you realized that perhaps

71
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,630
you could use her

72
00:07:58,630 --> 00:07:59,430
as a surrogate

73
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:01,040
to continue your family line.

74
00:08:01,830 --> 00:08:04,070
So you persuaded Sun Jiahao

75
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,000
to establish Luoda.

76
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:08,040
You fulfilled your wish.

77
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:10,830
Fan Tianci

78
00:08:11,870 --> 00:08:13,630
is the child born through surrogacy.

79
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:16,920
You people

80
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:24,680
keep spouting

81
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:28,480
your absurd ethical objections.

82
00:08:29,270 --> 00:08:31,600
But you have no idea

83
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:37,200
how much pain a person
with a physical impairment

84
00:08:38,390 --> 00:08:40,670
feels when unable

85
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:43,790
to fulfill their purpose.

86
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:48,750
They use

87
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:52,150
scientific methods

88
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:54,390
to pursue their goals.

89
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,750
What is wrong with that?

90
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,080
Organ transplantation

91
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:03,840
can

92
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:06,240
prolong life.

93
00:09:07,270 --> 00:09:08,360
Surrogacy

94
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,840
can create life.

95
00:09:15,670 --> 00:09:16,480
How

96
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,870
great

97
00:09:20,030 --> 00:09:21,480
and noble that is.

98
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:23,150
What about the surrogate mothers

99
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:24,960
who were deceived,

100
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:26,200
coerced,

101
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,270
and harmed?

102
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:33,030
They received fair compensation

103
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:37,150
and performed their natural duty
as women.

104
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:40,200
That's better than wasting

105
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:43,670
their lives and youth.

106
00:09:44,270 --> 00:09:46,790
They did it for society

107
00:09:47,270 --> 00:09:48,320
and for humanity.

108
00:09:49,270 --> 00:09:51,440
Your surrogacy factory
in Fanjia Village

109
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:54,030
served you alone.

110
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,080
Every surrogate mother there

111
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:58,960
was carrying your child.

112
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:05,120
My genes are superior

113
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,440
and have a greater right to live on.

114
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,270
You're wrong.

115
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:14,790
Your genes lack

116
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:17,600
the finest quality in human genetics:

117
00:10:21,390 --> 00:10:22,120
humanity.

118
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,670
We have found your surrogacy factory.

119
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,000
From now on,

120
00:10:35,270 --> 00:10:36,550
think carefully about

121
00:10:36,790 --> 00:10:39,120
how you'll atone to those you harmed.

122
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,750
You're wrong.

123
00:10:51,630 --> 00:10:53,440
I'm not the one at fault.

124
00:10:53,870 --> 00:11:00,080
Reproduction is civilization's mission.

125
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:05,790
It is a great act of creation.

126
00:11:16,030 --> 00:11:16,870
I'm afraid

127
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:18,870
Old Fan

128
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,030
won't be leaving with you.

129
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:22,750
And neither will you.

130
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,000
Alzheimer's disease usually progresses

131
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,790
over at least two years.

132
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:31,080
Fan Zhichang's sudden severe symptoms...

133
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,440
You poisoned him, didn't you?

134
00:11:32,870 --> 00:11:33,550
Mrs. Fan.

135
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:41,080
After he brought Tianci home,

136
00:11:41,630 --> 00:11:43,200
I knew what he was doing.

137
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,870
Tianci isn't related to you by blood.

138
00:11:48,870 --> 00:11:49,870
So you hated him?

139
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:53,440
I just wanted to protect him.

140
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,270
I didn't want him
to keep making mistakes.

141
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:01,600
Let's go.

142
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:36,910
Uncle He.
Hey.

143
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:50,150
Morning, Captain Ren.
Morning.

144
00:13:51,790 --> 00:13:53,870
How are the case briefing materials
coming?

145
00:13:54,550 --> 00:13:55,360
They're all ready.

146
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:57,840
Captain.
Morning.

147
00:13:58,910 --> 00:13:59,720
Where's Han Ning?

148
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:05,080
Captain Ren.

149
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,200
Everything is ready.

150
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:18,360
[Serve the People]

151
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:19,130
[This story is entirely fictional.]

152
00:14:19,140 --> 00:14:20,510
[The surrogacy depicted violates law,
ethics, and conscience.]

153
00:14:20,510 --> 00:14:22,100
[It violates women's personal rights
and tramples on human dignity.]

154
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:23,420
[We call on all viewers to reject
surrogacy in every form.]

155
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:24,600
[Together, uphold ethical boundaries,
the law, and social order.]

156
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:01,000
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

157
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,950
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

158
00:15:02,950 --> 00:15:04,860
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

159
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:06,670
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

160
00:15:06,670 --> 00:15:09,000
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

161
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,430
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

162
00:15:14,570 --> 00:15:16,480
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

163
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:18,380
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

164
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:20,320
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

165
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:22,450
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

166
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,460
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

167
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:26,620
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

168
00:15:30,210 --> 00:15:33,690
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

169
00:15:33,690 --> 00:15:37,060
♪Why is that child crying?♪

170
00:15:37,290 --> 00:15:39,760
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

171
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:41,380
♪Means I've grown up♪

172
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:44,530
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

173
00:15:44,530 --> 00:15:48,010
♪The wound still aches♪

174
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:52,770
♪Like a biting winter♪

175
00:15:52,770 --> 00:15:56,040
♪But a spark still glows♪

